  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn></math>&nbsp;similar drops of mercury are maintained at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>&nbsp;each. All these spherical drops combine into a single big drop. The potential energy of the bigger drop is ___________ times that of a smaller drop.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "243",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>27</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>r</mi></math></p><p>Potential energy of smaller drop&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>r</mi></mfrac></math></p><p>Potential energy of bigger drop :&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><msup><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>R</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>27</mn><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>R</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mi>k</mi><mfrac><mrow><mfenced><mn>27</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mn>27</mn></mfenced><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfenced><mn>27</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mn>27</mn></mfenced></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>r</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>243</mn><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math></p>",
